userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add coding-agent-owned public loop-handler types, a validated plugin extension, and a run-scoped registry getter.

**Motivation** — The P3 loop-event registry has no external registration surface; every steering or policy idea inside the agent loop must currently be merged into nax as a built-in.

**Approach** — Build once per run. `PluginRegistry.getLoopHandlers()` iterates `registry.plugins` (load order: global dir, project dir, `config.plugins[]`), keeps those whose `provides` includes `"loop-handlers"`, and calls each `register(on)` with a registrar that stages `{ plugin: plugin.name, event, handler }`. The result is `Object.freeze`d and memoised. A plugin's `register()` throwing drops that plugin's entries, logs a `plugins` warning naming the plugin, and continues; an unknown event likewise drops all that plugin's entries and warns with its name and the invalid event. Add `"loop-handlers"` to `PluginType` and `VALID_PLUGIN_TYPES`; when declared, `validatePlugin` calls a new `validateLoopHandlers(pluginName, ext)` beside `validatePostRunAction`, requiring `extensions.loopHandlers` to be an object with a function `register`. Export public types from `loop-events/index.ts`; `src/plugins/` imports coding-agent types, never the reverse.

**Scope** — In: plugin declarations, validation, registration ordering/atomicity, memoization and type exports. Out: US-002 invocation/timeout wrapper; US-003 installation into turns; US-004 run/session forwarding; Declarative per-role or per-stage filters on a registration; plugin handlers scope themselves by reading `LoopHandlerContext` at runtime. Unsubscribing a handler, registering handlers per turn or per story, and any `LoopHandlerContext` capability beyond read-only facts (no abort, no UI, no config access). Extracting the coding agent into a standalone package; this slice only cuts the types so that move stays mechanical.

**Interface** — In `src/agents/native/session/loop-events/types.ts` (exported from `loop-events/index.ts`):
```ts
export interface LoopHandlerContext {
  readonly sessionName: string;
  readonly role?: string;
  readonly storyId?: string;
  readonly feature?: string;
  readonly workdir?: string;
  readonly model?: string;
  readonly provider?: string;
}

export type ExternalHandlerOf<E extends LoopEvent> = (
  payload: PayloadOf<E>,
  ctx: LoopHandlerContext,
) => PatchOf<E> | undefined | Promise<PatchOf<E> | undefined>;

export interface LoopHandlerEntry {
  readonly plugin: string;
  readonly event: LoopEvent;
  readonly handler: ExternalHandlerOf<LoopEvent>;
}

export type LoopHandlerSet = readonly LoopHandlerEntry[];
```
In `src/plugins/extensions.ts`:
```ts
export type LoopHandlerRegistrar = <E extends LoopEvent>(event: E, handler: ExternalHandlerOf<E>) => void;

export interface ILoopHandlerProvider {
  register(on: LoopHandlerRegistrar): void;
}
```
`PluginExtensions` gains `loopHandlers?: ILoopHandlerProvider`; `PluginRegistry` gains `getLoopHandlers(): LoopHandlerSet`.

**Goal** — Safely invoke external loop handlers with current context, bounded lifetime and event-specific failure behavior.

**Motivation** — `src/hooks/` fires around a story, shells out with a 5s timeout and cannot return a patch; in-process external handlers must not hang a turn or silently allow a failed tool guard.

**Approach** — `wrapExternalHandler(entry, getCtx, signal)` in the new `src/agents/native/session/loop-events/external-handler.ts` returns a built-in `HandlerOf<E>` that calls `entry.handler(payload, getCtx())` and composes, as an ordered pipeline:
1. race the handler's settlement against a `LOOP_HANDLER_TIMEOUT_MS` (10_000) timer and the `signal`'s abort — the first to settle wins, later settlements are discarded, and the timer is cleared once the race settles;
2. a throw, rejection, timeout or abort is a **failure**;
3. on `before_tool` only, a settled value that is not an object with a `kind` of `allow`, `nudge`, `block` or `terminate` — other than `undefined` — is a **failure**;
4. a settled `undefined` becomes `{ kind: "allow" }` on `before_tool` and `{}` on every other event;
5. a failure on `before_tool` returns `{ kind: "block", isError: true, content: "Blocked: loop handler from plugin '<plugin>' failed (<reason>)." }` and logs `native-loop-events` warn with `{ plugin, event, tool, error }`; a failure on any other event returns `{}` and logs `native-loop-events` warn with `{ plugin, event, error }`. The wrapper never rethrows;
6. a successful patch carrying any of `seed`, `history`, `messages` or `summary` is logged at debug with `{ plugin, event, fields }` so a later `applyHistoryPatch` rejection can be traced.
The timeout is read through `_externalHandlerDeps.timeoutMs` so tests can shorten it. `dispatchBeforeTool` must treat a built-in outcome not an object carrying a `kind` as `{ kind: "allow" }` with a `native-loop-events` warning, rather than dereferencing `kind` outside its try. Keep dispatcher patch-field picking, array restoration, cache-boundary history rejection and follow-up cap intact.

**Scope** — In: wrapper, timeout test seam, failure logs, malformed dispatcher return guard. Out: US-003 installation and adapter plumbing; US-004 delivery through session manager; A timeout on built-in loop handlers; only plugin handlers are timed. Freezing nested payload objects; plugin handlers get the same readonly-typed, array-restored payloads built-ins get. Changes to the dispatcher's history cache-boundary rule, the `MAX_FOLLOW_UPS_PER_TURN` cap, or the patchable-field lists. Configuring the plugin handler timeout through `NaxConfig`; it is the constant `LOOP_HANDLER_TIMEOUT_MS`.

**Interface** — `wrapExternalHandler(entry, getCtx, signal)` returns `HandlerOf<E>`; export `LOOP_HANDLER_TIMEOUT_MS = 10_000` and `_externalHandlerDeps.timeoutMs` from `src/agents/native/session/loop-events/external-handler.ts`. Use the US-001 `LoopHandlerEntry`, `LoopHandlerContext` and `ExternalHandlerOf<E>` interfaces without importing `src/plugins/` into native code.
